Assemble the Wi-Fi Duck

To connect the ESP8266 and ATmega32U4, we'll be working with a breadboard and jumper wires. So place each MCU on the breadboard, then use jumper wires to make the following pin connections.

    D1 or GPIO 5 (ESP8266) to 3 or SCL (ATmega32U4)
    D2 or GPIO 4 (ESP8266) to 2 or SDA (ATmega32U4)
    GND (ESP8266) to GND (ATmega32U4)
    5V (ESP8266) to RAW (ATmega32U4)

If you have a NeoPixel LED, also make these connections:

    VCC (NeoPixel) to VCC (ATmega32U4)
    GND (NeoPixel) to GND (ATmega32U4)
    DI (NeoPixel) to 7 (ATmega32U4)

